extends RefCounted
## Enemy definitions. All values are tuned for "friendly but real" combat.
## telegraph = seconds of visible/audible wind-up before an attack lands (readable attacks).
## recover   = seconds the enemy is open to punishment after attacking.
## Damage is scaled at runtime by horror intensity for underground threats (see data/horror_events.gd INTENSITY).
## Chapter Two entries (docs/CHAPTER_TWO_SPEC.md 4.5; appended, legacy entries never change) add:
##   areas        every area id the enemy appears in (`area` = its home/primary area)
##   zones        zone ids of its authored pockets (NEW spawner ids only, e.g. hr_sp_orchard_mimics)
##   attacks      [{id, kind, telegraph, damage, recover, tell, ...}] - every attack's readable wind-up and
##                visual tell (the tell text doubles as the caption with sound muted). kind: charge | bite |
##                projectile | swing | scrape | leap | roll | sweep | throw | dash | drain | pulse | root_sweep |
##                roots | hazard | channel | zone (a boss's delayed strike zones)
##   elite / boss  larger authored encounters (drops are guaranteed materials; story items come from rewards)
##   underground  true: horror intensity scales its damage like the legacy "below" enemies
##   front_armor  damage taken from the front is multiplied by (1 - front_armor) (never immune)
##   max_group    most of this enemy alive in one authored encounter
##   alt_name/alt_sound  arachnophobia replacements for spider-like enemies (different silhouette too)
##   sound        an EXISTING voice prefix (Audio PREFIX_FALLBACK) so every enemy is audible today;
##   voice / alt_voice  the dedicated voice prefix the audio module should add for this enemy (then point
##                `sound` at it). Every attack tell is also visual, so nothing depends on sound.
## Stat ranges follow MP sections 12/13. No drop is ever the only source of a story-required item.

